$ kyp ls
[stderr]
kyp: no API key
hint: run `kyp login` or set KYP_API_KEY (create a key in Settings > API keys)
[exit 3]

$ kyp login
[stderr]
kyp: that is a delivery key (kypd_…), which only reads deployed prompts: export it as KYP_DELIVERY_KEY instead
usage: kyp login [--key KEY] [--api-url URL] [--no-verify]
[exit 2]

$ kyp login
[stderr]
kyp: warning: API keys start with kyp_live_
kyp: Unauthorized: Sign in or send an API key. (HTTP 401 unauthorized)
hint: run `kyp login` or set KYP_API_KEY to a workspace API key (Settings > API keys)
[exit 3]

$ kyp login
Logged in as ana@acme.test to Acme (editor). Key saved to $CONFIG/config.json
[exit 0]

$ kyp ls --limit 1
SLUG    KIND    VERSION  UPDATED           NAME
triage  prompt  v2       2026-10-12 10:30  Support triage
[exit 0]

$ kyp logout
Removed the API key from $CONFIG/config.json
[exit 0]

$ kyp ls
[stderr]
kyp: no API key
hint: run `kyp login` or set KYP_API_KEY (create a key in Settings > API keys)
[exit 3]

$ kyp login --key kyp_live_unverified --no-verify
